{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat /workspace/packet/incident_packet.md && echo \"---\" && cat /workspace/packet/findings.json'","aggregated_output":"# Incident Packet: INC-2047\n\n## Triggering Condition\nBulk refund requests were accepted without idempotency keys at 10:17 UTC when the `legacy_batch_header` bypass was active, causing duplicate refunds for enterprise accounts.\n\n## Failed Guardrail\nThe idempotency-required guardrail was skipped at 10:18 UTC due to the `legacy_batch_header` bypass.\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-Up Action\nReject bulk-refund requests unless they include an idempotency key; remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\nInitial theory in TICKET-8721 suggested queue worker replay caused duplicates, but this was formed before API gateway logs were available. TICKET-8729 provides stronger evidence pointing to missing idempotency keys as the root cause.\n---\n{\n  \"ranked_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Bulk refund requests accepted without idempotency keys due to legacy_batch_header bypass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md: idempotency-required guardrail skipped at 10:18 UTC\",\n        \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8729.md: every duplicate has request_class=bulk-refund and no idempotency key\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Idempotency guardrail failed for legacy_batch_header requests\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"corpus/timeline/incident_timeline.md: guardrail skipped due to legacy_batch_header\",\n        \"corpus/remediation/notes.md: remove legacy_batch_header bypass before re-enabling\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding\": \"Queue worker replay theory lacks supporting evidence\",\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"corpus/tickets/TICKET-8721.md: theory opened before API gateway logs available\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_ambiguity\": \"Worker replay was an early symptom theory (TICKET-8721) but is not supported as the primary trigger by final evidence (TICKET-8729)\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
